<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="AL_TO_ALR" Comment="Composite FB for converting AL (LWORD) adapter to ALR (LREAL) adapter — ⚠&#10;BIT-REINTERPRETATION, NOT a numeric cast! A raw counter/analog value is&#10;misinterpreted as IEEE754 bits. See AD_TO_AR_TODO.md / AD_TO_AR_NUM for the safe&#10;two-stage (bit-string-&gt;int-&gt;real) alternative.">
	<Identification Standard="61499-2" Description="Copyright (c) 2026 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2026-02-17">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="adapter::conversion::unidirectional">
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<Plugs>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="ALR_OUT" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::ALR" Comment="LREAL Adapter Output" x="2300" y="0"/>
		</Plugs>
		<Sockets>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="AL_IN" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AL" Comment="LWORD Adapter Input" x="0" y="0"/>
		</Sockets>
	</InterfaceList>
	<FBNetwork>
		<FB Name="Convert" Type="iec61131::conversion::F_LWORD_TO_LREAL" x="1000" y="0">
		</FB>
		<EventConnections>
			<Connection Source="AL_IN.E1" Destination="Convert.REQ" dx1="100"/>
			<Connection Source="Convert.CNF" Destination="ALR_OUT.E1" dx1="100"/>
		</EventConnections>
		<DataConnections>
			<Connection Source="AL_IN.D1" Destination="Convert.IN" dx1="100"/>
			<Connection Source="Convert.OUT" Destination="ALR_OUT.D1" dx1="100"/>
		</DataConnections>
	</FBNetwork>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>AL_TO_ALR</h1>

<h2>🇩🇪 Deutsch</h2>

<p><strong>⚠️ Achtung:</strong> Dieser Baustein wandelt LWORD nicht numerisch in LREAL um, sondern nutzt intern <code>F_LWORD_TO_LREAL</code>, was im FORTE-Kern für Bit-String-Quelltypen (BYTE/WORD/DWORD/LWORD) eine reine IEEE754-Bit-Reinterpretation ist — dieselbe Falle wie bei <code>AD_TO_AR</code> (DWORD→REAL), hier nur mit den 64-bit-Pendants LWORD/LREAL. Ein roher Zähler-/Analogwert würde dadurch NICHT in den entsprechenden REAL-Zahlenwert umgewandelt, sondern ergäbe eine bedeutungslose Zahl.</p>

<p><code>AL_TO_ALR</code> ist trotzdem korrekt, wenn <code>AL_IN</code> bereits ein Bitmuster ist, das als LREAL interpretiert werden soll (z. B. das Ergebnis eines <code>F_LREAL_TO_LWORD</code>).</p>

<p><strong>Für einen echten Zahlenwert</strong>: zweistufig über <code>AL_TO_AULI</code> (Bit-Reinterpretation LWORD→ULINT, hier gültig, da beide dieselbe 64-bit-Darstellung eines vorzeichenlosen Integers teilen) gefolgt von <code>AULI_TO_ALR</code> (echter numerischer Cast) — dasselbe Muster wie <code>AD_TO_AR_NUM</code> für den 32-bit-Fall.</p>

<h2>🇬🇧 English</h2>

<p><strong>⚠️ Warning:</strong> This block does not numerically convert LWORD to LREAL — it internally uses <code>F_LWORD_TO_LREAL</code>, which in the FORTE core is a pure IEEE754 bit-reinterpretation for bit-string source types (BYTE/WORD/DWORD/LWORD) — the same trap as <code>AD_TO_AR</code> (DWORD→REAL), here with the 64-bit counterparts LWORD/LREAL. A raw counter/analog value would NOT become the corresponding REAL number, but a meaningless value.</p>

<p><code>AL_TO_ALR</code> is still correct when <code>AL_IN</code> is already a bit pattern meant to be interpreted as LREAL (e.g. the result of an <code>F_LREAL_TO_LWORD</code>).</p>

<p><strong>For an actual numeric value</strong>: chain <code>AL_TO_AULI</code> (bit-reinterpretation LWORD→ULINT, valid here since both share the same 64-bit unsigned-integer representation) followed by <code>AULI_TO_ALR</code> (a real numeric cast) — the same pattern as <code>AD_TO_AR_NUM</code> for the 32-bit case.</p>
]]></Attribute>
</FBType>
